{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792714350,"nonce":"KbeuiRx690usz6rKubp9ky+aRJA=","message":"Confirmed the live single-window RayDE process itself at 508.0 MiB footprint (peak 518.0 MiB); its saved session had 38 tabs. This excludes Apple Open/Save helper processes.\n\nA matched native AOT probe visits 65 generated Haxe files, closes all tabs and samples physical footprint via memory_probe.py. Pre-multiwindow: baseline 105.2 MiB, tabs open 299.4 MiB, closed idle 200.5 MiB. Regressed multiwindow: 110.4, 395.0, 292.2 MiB. The identical post-multiwindow executable with the native menu fix: 108.1, 331.0, 209.1 MiB. CoreAnimation regions while open fall from 3860 to 84 (pre-multiwindow 20).\n\nThe regression is macOS menu installation replacing NSApp.mainMenu on every active-tab/dirty/focus update. Ashui d0932fd34acdc2fedbed152ff4a3684186319289 updates existing NSMenu/NSMenuItem objects in place and bounds temporary autoreleased objects. The pin is adopted in scripts/deps.sh. Native tests cover identity across 200 updates, shortcut/enabled changes, action dispatch, separators and submenu insertion/removal.\n\nThe broader memory issue remains open: fixed 331.0 MiB does not yet equal the earlier 299.4 MiB matched baseline or the reported 310 MB benchmark. Managed occupied blocks varied between runs, so this does not attribute the remaining gap to the menu layer. Artifacts: bin/window-memory-regression-before, bin/window-memory-regression-after and bin/window-memory-regression-fixed; probe source tests/WindowMemoryProbe.hx.","files":null}]}